        "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b3496ddcaeaf1c88b9dc44910e7d266db4415d4b.001.1",
        "event": "Frost Advisory",
        "headline": "Frost Advisory issued September 1 at 1:22PM AKDT until September 2 at 9:00AM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Temperatures as low as 28 degrees will result in frost\nformation.\n\n* WHERE...Colder locations throughout the Anchorage Bowl and Lower\nMatanuska Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 AM AKDT Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Frost could harm sensitive outdoor vegetation. Sensitive\noutdoor plants may be killed if left uncovered.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The cold airmass and clear skies observed this\nmorning are expected again tonight through early Wednesday morning.\nMany areas of Anchorage and the Matanuska Val",
        "severity": "Minor",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Anchorage AK",
        "effective": "2026-09-01T13:22:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-09-02T09:00:00-08:00",
        "areas": "Anchorage; Lower Matanuska Valley",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Prepare",
        "instruction": "Take steps now to protect tender plants from the cold.",
        "lat": null,
        "lng": null
      },
      {
        "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1b2bb1a13eb772f0915c82b1a1697d9a0e4bcc6b.001.1",
        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued September 1 at 2:30AM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Snow. Total snow accumulations of 3 to 6 inches above\n2000 feet and 1 to 3 inches below 2000 feet, with higher amounts\nabove pass level. Winds could gust as high as 30 mph over\nAtigun Pass Tuesday night.\n\n* WHERE...Central/Eastern Brooks Range and Eastern Arctic Coast.\n\n* WHEN...Tuesday September 1st through Wednesday September 2nd.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be difficult. Gusty winds could lead to\nareas of blowing snow which could significantly reduce\nvisibility.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS..",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Observed",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "effective": "2026-09-01T02:30:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-09-01T16:00:00-08:00",
        "areas": "Eastern Beaufort Sea Coast; Central Brooks Range; Romanzof Mountains",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Execute",
        "instruction": "Slow down and use caution while traveling. Visit 511.alaska.gov or\ncall 5 1 1 for the latest road conditions.",
        "lat": null,
        "lng": null
      }
    ]
